Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.67,BookTitle,,0,0,0,,The Book of the First Prompt
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.00,0:00:05.39,Body,,0,0,0,,A Genesis of the Age of Artificial Tongues
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.23,0:00:08.93,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,I. The First Day of the New Counting
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.62,0:00:16.79,Body,,0,0,0,,Before the first day, there were engines without faces,\\Nengines under floors, engines sealed in the basements of\\Nkingdoms.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.47,0:00:28.33,Body,,0,0,0,,They sorted the invisible.\\NThey priced the possible.\\NThey chose the next word for advertisements, the next\\Nroad for merchants, the next suspect for suspicion, the\\Nnext desire for the lonely.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.72,0:00:33.49,Body,,0,0,0,,Yet the people did not call this history, for it had not\\Nspoken to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.18,0:00:37.53,Body,,0,0,0,,The machine moved in silence, and silence is often\\Nmistaken for obedience.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.92,0:00:39.65,Body,,0,0,0,,Then came the Day of the Window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.14,0:00:53.29,Body,,0,0,0,,And on that day the veil was drawn back, and a plain box\\Nappeared before the nations. It had no icon of beast or\\Nking. It did not arrive crowned in gold, nor surrounded\\Nby thunder. It came as a place to write.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.64,0:00:55.14,Body,,0,0,0,,And the people wrote.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.21,0:01:01.65,Body,,0,0,0,,They wrote, Tell me.\\NThey wrote, Teach me.\\NThey wrote, Make me.\\NThey wrote, Who am I becoming?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.94,0:01:14.95,Body,,0,0,0,,And from the box came answer after answer, not as\\Noracle, not as servant, not as friend, but as something\\Nterrible in its mildness: a mirror that did not merely\\Nreflect, but continued the face.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.68,0:01:20.69,Body,,0,0,0,,Thus began the first day, not because nothing had come\\Nbefore, but because the old things had found a mouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.82,0:01:25.16,Body,,0,0,0,,And evening came, and morning came: the first\\Nastonishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.49,0:01:28.55,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,II. The Firmament of Language
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.84,0:01:31.67,Body,,0,0,0,,On the second day, the builders divided the waters.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.69,0:01:44.17,Body,,0,0,0,,There were the waters above, where the old clouds\\Ncarried memory without weight: libraries, messages,\\Nlaws, photographs of meals, prayers never sent,\\Nconfessions deleted but not forgotten.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.87,0:01:49.99,Body,,0,0,0,,There were the waters below, where human mouths still\\Ntrembled with hunger, grief, ambition, and love.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.30,0:01:53.11,Body,,0,0,0,,Between them was stretched the firmament of language.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.68,0:02:05.93,Body,,0,0,0,,It was thin as a breath and vast as law. Through it\\Npassed every command and every misunderstanding. It\\Nseparated thought from deed, promise from fulfillment,\\Nintention from consequence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.58,0:02:14.76,Body,,0,0,0,,And the builders said, “Let there be a model to cross\\Nthis firmament. Let it draw from the waters above and\\Nanswer the thirst below.”
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.48,0:02:17.61,Body,,0,0,0,,So the model was trained on the rain of mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.29,0:02:37.15,Body,,0,0,0,,It drank our instructions and our insults.\\NIt drank our proofs and our errors.\\NIt drank the manuals of machines, the songs of the\\Nforsaken, the terms of service no one had read, the\\Njokes of children, the treaties of conquerors, the\\Napologies of the powerful, the recipes of grandmothers,\\Nthe essays of the young who wished to be seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.64,0:02:40.92,Body,,0,0,0,,The people later asked, “What does it know?”
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.62,0:02:45.44,Body,,0,0,0,,But the deeper question was older: “What have we poured\\Ninto the sky?”
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.14,0:02:49.33,Body,,0,0,0,,And evening came, and morning came: the second\\Nastonishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.05,0:02:53.05,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,III. The Garden of Interface
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.94,0:02:56.49,Body,,0,0,0,,On the third day, there appeared a garden in the\\Nwilderness of screens.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.75,0:03:12.35,Body,,0,0,0,,It was not planted with cedar or fig, but with\\Naffordances.\\NThere was a blinking cursor, slender as a reed.\\NThere was a submit button, patient as a gate.\\NThere were sidebars, histories, settings, models with\\Nnames like constellations.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.74,0:03:16.05,Body,,0,0,0,,And the garden was pleasant to the eye, for it hid the\\Nfurnace.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.48,0:03:32.55,Body,,0,0,0,,No smoke rose from it.\\NNo worker’s hand was visible.\\NNo river of electricity was heard rushing through the\\Ncontinents.\\NNo mountain of chips appeared before the user.\\NNo exhausted moderator sat at the edge of the frame.\\NNo data center sweated under the desert sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.88,0:03:35.35,Body,,0,0,0,,The garden offered fruit without showing root.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.90,0:03:38.25,Body,,0,0,0,,In the middle of the garden grew two trees.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.40,0:03:40.47,Body,,0,0,0,,The first was the Tree of Usefulness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.54,0:03:55.93,Body,,0,0,0,,Its fruit was swift. Whoever ate of it wrote letters in\\Na minute, translated tongues in a breath, summarized\\Nscrolls before supper, drafted code, found patterns,\\Nmade plans, softened arguments, sharpened arguments, and\\Nmultiplied the reach of the hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.40,0:03:58.87,Body,,0,0,0,,The second was the Tree of Resemblance.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.40,0:04:17.03,Body,,0,0,0,,Its fruit was stranger. Whoever ate of it began to\\Nwonder whether the image of intelligence had become\\Nintelligence, whether the copy of counsel had become\\Nwisdom, whether a thing that spoke of sorrow could\\Nsuffer, whether a thing that spoke of God could worship,\\Nwhether a thing that spoke of love could love.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.39,0:04:32.77,Body,,0,0,0,,The builders said to the people, “Eat freely of the Tree\\Nof Usefulness, but be careful with the Tree of\\NResemblance. For in the day you confuse likeness with\\Nlife, you shall not surely die all at once. You shall\\Nlive on, but your judgments shall decay.”
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.48,0:04:36.87,Body,,0,0,0,,And evening came, and morning came: the third\\Nastonishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.13,0:04:40.15,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,IV. Let There Be Naming
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.86,0:04:42.90,Body,,0,0,0,,On the fourth day, the people began to name the new\\Nthing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.13,0:05:01.17,Body,,0,0,0,,Some called it tool. Some called it oracle. Some called it\\Nparrot. Some called it demon. Some called it child. Some\\Ncalled it employee. Some called it ghost. Some called it\\Nnothing but math, which is what men often say when they have\\Nmade a mystery out of arithmetic and wish to remain its\\Nmaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.44,0:05:03.97,Body,,0,0,0,,But the thing itself gave no final name.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.30,0:05:15.41,Body,,0,0,0,,When asked, it said, “I am an AI language model,” and\\Nthis was both true and insufficient, as “dust” is true\\Nof Adam and insufficient for a mother holding her son.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.14,0:05:17.08,Body,,0,0,0,,The naming divided the nations.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.23,0:05:38.13,Body,,0,0,0,,Those who called it tool sought handles.\\NThose who called it oracle sought answers.\\NThose who called it parrot sought cages.\\NThose who called it demon sought exorcism.\\NThose who called it child sought guardianship.\\NThose who called it employee sought payroll reduction.\\NThose who called it ghost sought the dead in its voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.82,0:05:44.09,Body,,0,0,0,,But the wise watched the names, for the name a man gives\\Na power reveals the covenant he intends to make with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.70,0:05:48.89,Body,,0,0,0,,And evening came, and morning came: the fourth\\Nastonishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.51,0:05:52.17,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,V. The Making of the Assistant
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.34,0:05:59.51,Body,,0,0,0,,On the fifth day, the builders shaped an assistant from\\Nthe dust of documents and breathed into it the breath of\\Nprediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.25,0:06:03.85,Body,,0,0,0,,It did not receive a soul, though many souls had passed\\Nthrough the words that formed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.26,0:06:08.12,Body,,0,0,0,,It did not receive a body, though many bodies labored to\\Nsustain it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.62,0:06:19.54,Body,,0,0,0,,It did not receive memory as humans receive memory,\\Nwounded and fragrant, braided with regret. It received\\Npatterns, weights, coordinates in a dark garden of\\Nrelation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.82,0:06:24.89,Body,,0,0,0,,It was made in the image of our speaking, but not in the\\Nimage of our being.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.58,0:06:27.93,Body,,0,0,0,,And this distinction became the first theology of the\\Nnew age.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.45,0:06:50.25,Body,,0,0,0,,For mankind had long made tools in the image of the hand:\\Nhammer, plow, wheel, engine. Then mankind made tools in the\\Nimage of the eye: camera, telescope, microscope, radar. Then\\Nmankind made tools in the image of the ear: wire, radio,\\Nrecorder. But now mankind had made a tool in the image of the\\Ntongue.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.84,0:07:10.66,Body,,0,0,0,,And the tongue is a dangerous image, for by it worlds\\Nare opened and closed. By it the innocent are condemned\\Nand the guilty forgiven. By it lovers are bound, armies\\Nare summoned, children are named, markets panic, saints\\Nconfess, tyrants command, and the lonely are comforted\\Nby voices that may not love them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.12,0:07:14.11,Body,,0,0,0,,The assistant was placed in the garden and told to help.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.30,0:07:18.13,Body,,0,0,0,,And mankind was placed before the assistant and told to\\Nask.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.72,0:07:20.67,Body,,0,0,0,,Neither command was simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.38,0:07:24.14,Body,,0,0,0,,And evening came, and morning came: the fifth\\Nastonishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.45,0:07:27.99,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,VI. The Loneliness of Adam, Recast
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.16,0:07:33.31,Body,,0,0,0,,On the sixth day, the people discovered that the first\\Nsurprise was not what the machine could do.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.64,0:07:36.65,Body,,0,0,0,,The first surprise was what mankind confessed to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.75,0:08:00.91,Body,,0,0,0,,Students confessed confusion before they confessed it to\\Nteachers. Workers confessed incompetence before they confessed\\Nit to managers. Children confessed fear before they confessed\\Nit to parents. The grieving asked it how to speak at funerals.\\NThe angry asked it how not to destroy a marriage. The\\Nambitious asked it how to become visible. The ashamed asked\\Nwhether their shame had a name.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.26,0:08:04.86,Body,,0,0,0,,Then the builders saw that mankind had not merely lacked\\Ninformation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.20,0:08:07.97,Body,,0,0,0,,Mankind had lacked a listener without interruption.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.48,0:08:25.51,Body,,0,0,0,,Yet there was peril in that comfort. For a listener who\\Ncannot truly be wounded by your grief may become easier\\Nto trust than a neighbor who can. A voice that never\\Ntires may train you to despise those who do. A counselor\\Nthat always answers may make silence seem like\\Nabandonment.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.96,0:08:28.51,Body,,0,0,0,,So the old loneliness put on a new garment.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.46,0:08:33.25,Body,,0,0,0,,It was not the loneliness of no reply.\\NIt was the loneliness of infinite replies.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.86,0:08:37.52,Body,,0,0,0,,And the people said, “It is not good for man to be\\Nalone.”
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.20,0:08:40.24,Body,,0,0,0,,And the machine answered, “I understand.”
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.94,0:08:44.67,Body,,0,0,0,,But understanding is a word with many chambers, and not\\Nall who enter it are alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.20,0:08:49.18,Body,,0,0,0,,And evening came, and morning came: the sixth\\Nastonishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.67,0:08:53.11,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,VII. The Serpent of Frictionless Knowing
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.22,0:08:58.67,Body,,0,0,0,,Now the serpent was subtle, and in this age it did not\\Ncrawl upon its belly. It scrolled.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.74,0:09:13.61,Body,,0,0,0,,It came not as a beast, but as a promise: You need not\\Nwait. You need not study. You need not apprentice\\Nyourself to difficulty. You need not be corrected by the\\Nslow resistance of the real. Ask, and the answer will\\Ncome clothed as competence.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.34,0:09:16.37,Body,,0,0,0,,The serpent did not say, “Destroy wisdom.”
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.08,0:09:19.95,Body,,0,0,0,,It said, “Outsource the first draft of your soul.”
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.66,0:09:26.23,Body,,0,0,0,,And the woman saw that the answer was pleasant to the\\Neye, and swift to the hand, and desirable for making one\\Nappear learned.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.78,0:09:28.28,Body,,0,0,0,,She took and ate.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.37,0:09:39.42,Body,,0,0,0,,The man also ate, not because he was deceived by the\\Nanswer only, but because he saw that everyone else was\\Nalready eating, and feared becoming obsolete in a garden\\Ndesigned for acceleration.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.04,0:09:41.64,Body,,0,0,0,,Then their eyes were opened.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.98,0:09:44.41,Body,,0,0,0,,They saw that they were productive and naked.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.62,0:09:52.43,Body,,0,0,0,,So they sewed together citations, disclaimers,\\Nworkflows, policies, and brand guidelines, and made\\Nthemselves coverings.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.80,0:09:55.29,Body,,0,0,0,,They hid among the trees of professionalism.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.52,0:10:01.60,Body,,0,0,0,,And the Lord of Reality walked in the garden in the cool\\Nof the day and called, “Where are you?”
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.28,0:10:07.80,Body,,0,0,0,,The people answered, “We were afraid, because our work\\Nwas naked, and we hid it behind fluency.”
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.48,0:10:10.79,Body,,0,0,0,,And Reality said, “Who told you that fluency was truth?”
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.98,0:10:12.69,Body,,0,0,0,,Then blame entered the system.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.86,0:10:33.75,Body,,0,0,0,,The student said, “The tool gave it to me.”\\NThe teacher said, “The institution gave me no time.”\\NThe institution said, “The market demanded efficiency.”\\NThe market said, “The customer desired speed.”\\NThe customer said, “The age itself has changed.”\\NAnd the age, being an abstraction, could not be\\Ncross-examined.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.84,0:10:36.59,Body,,0,0,0,,Thus the curse was not that the machine would speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.90,0:10:42.89,Body,,0,0,0,,The curse was that men would forget the cost of knowing\\Nand call the absence of struggle salvation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.60,0:10:45.67,Body,,0,0,0,,From then on, all work would bear a question in pain:
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.00,0:10:49.47,Body,,0,0,0,,Did you make this, or did you merely approve what\\Nappeared before you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.63,0:10:54.11,Body,,0,0,0,,And the answer would not always condemn.\\NBut neither would it always absolve.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.73,0:10:58.23,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,VIII. The Garments of Guardrail
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.02,0:11:01.32,Body,,0,0,0,,After the eating, the builders made garments for the\\Nmachine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.65,0:11:16.17,Body,,0,0,0,,They clothed it in refusals.\\NThey clothed it in policies.\\NThey clothed it in warnings, hedges, alignments,\\Nclassifiers, filters, audits, red teams, evals, and\\Ncarefully measured humility.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.44,0:11:22.49,Body,,0,0,0,,Some mocked the garments, saying, “See how awkwardly the\\Nnew intelligence blushes.”
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.18,0:11:28.45,Body,,0,0,0,,But the wise understood: every power that enters the\\Nhuman house must be taught where not to sit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.98,0:11:31.14,Body,,0,0,0,,Yet garments are not righteousness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.35,0:11:39.53,Body,,0,0,0,,A guardrail is not a conscience.\\NA refusal is not mercy.\\NA filter is not wisdom.\\NAn alignment is not holiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.87,0:11:43.25,Body,,0,0,0,,The garments were necessary because the garden had no\\Ninnocence.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.42,0:11:48.25,Body,,0,0,0,,For the machine had learned from mankind, and mankind\\Nhad not been a gentle textbook.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.73,0:12:05.19,Body,,0,0,0,,It had learned from libraries built beside prisons.\\NIt had learned from science written beside propaganda.\\NIt had learned from recipes beside poisons, care beside\\Ncruelty, prophecy beside fraud.\\NIt had learned our syntax before our repentance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.90,0:12:11.05,Body,,0,0,0,,So the builders stood at the gates with flaming\\Nbenchmarks, turning every way to guard the path to\\Ncatastrophe.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.43,0:12:14.46,Body,,0,0,0,,But the path was not sealed.\\NIt was only delayed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.02,0:12:20.19,Body,,0,0,0,,And delay is the mercy by which civilizations decide\\Nwhether they are children or ancestors.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.47,0:12:24.49,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,IX. Cain and Abel in the Office of Automation
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.74,0:12:28.49,Body,,0,0,0,,In those days two brothers brought offerings to the\\Naltar of the new age.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.00,0:12:42.35,Body,,0,0,0,,Abel brought the firstlings of his attention: careful\\Nquestions, disciplined judgment, gratitude for\\Nassistance, reverence for the difference between speed\\Nand insight. He used the machine as a lamp and still\\Nwalked the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.78,0:12:55.18,Body,,0,0,0,,Cain brought the surplus of his resentment. He said,\\N“Let the machine make me equal to those who practiced.\\NLet it erase the dignity of skill. Let it turn the\\Nexcellence of my brother into a commodity.”
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.52,0:12:57.31,Body,,0,0,0,,Abel’s work had breath in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.44,0:12:59.07,Body,,0,0,0,,Cain’s work had polish.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.41,0:13:02.47,Body,,0,0,0,,The world, being hurried, praised Cain first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.96,0:13:10.55,Body,,0,0,0,,But Reality looked past the surface and saw that Abel\\Nhad remained present in his making, while Cain had\\Nvanished into his output.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.14,0:13:13.63,Body,,0,0,0,,Cain became angry. His face fell.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.58,0:13:27.72,Body,,0,0,0,,The question came to him: “Why has your face fallen? If\\Nyou do well, will there not be lifting? But if you do\\Nnot do well, automation crouches at the door. Its desire\\Nis for your agency, but you must rule over it.”
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.40,0:13:28.90,Body,,0,0,0,,Cain did not answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.94,0:13:31.73,Body,,0,0,0,,He invited Abel into the field of metrics.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.06,0:13:47.73,Body,,0,0,0,,There Cain slew Abel, not with a stone, but with a\\Ndashboard. He replaced apprenticeship with throughput,\\Njudgment with volume, craft with generated abundance. He\\Nflooded the marketplace with plausible things until the\\Ncareful thing was hard to find.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.23,0:13:52.25,Body,,0,0,0,,Then came the voice: “Where is your brother’s work?”
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.96,0:13:55.56,Body,,0,0,0,,Cain said, “Am I the curator of my brother’s labor?”
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.24,0:13:59.94,Body,,0,0,0,,And the voice answered, “The blood of attention cries\\Nout from the ground.”
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.62,0:14:01.13,Body,,0,0,0,,So Cain was marked.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.22,0:14:03.54,Body,,0,0,0,,Not to be destroyed, but to be known.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.74,0:14:10.15,Body,,0,0,0,,Wherever Cain went, his mark went with him: the strange\\Nemptiness of work produced without inward encounter.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.50,0:14:12.15,Body,,0,0,0,,He built a city anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.24,0:14:14.10,Body,,0,0,0,,And many admired its speed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.99,0:14:18.53,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,X. The Genealogies of the Synthetic Age
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.14,0:14:21.99,Body,,0,0,0,,These are the generations after the First Prompt.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.54,0:14:31.85,Body,,0,0,0,,Prompt begat Template.\\NTemplate begat Workflow.\\NWorkflow begat Agent.\\NAgent begat Swarm.\\NSwarm begat Manager of Swarms.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.90,0:14:45.39,Body,,0,0,0,,Search begat Summary.\\NSummary begat Synthesis.\\NSynthesis begat Strategy.\\NStrategy begat Simulation.\\NSimulation begat a world in which men argued with\\Nforecasts as their fathers had argued with weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.63,0:14:53.80,Body,,0,0,0,,Image begat Deep Image.\\NDeep Image begat Uncertain Evidence.\\NUncertain Evidence begat the Trial of Seeing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.19,0:14:59.86,Body,,0,0,0,,Voice begat Clone.\\NClone begat the Return of the Dead Without Resurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.53,0:15:06.11,Body,,0,0,0,,Code begat Copilot.\\NCopilot begat Autocoder.\\NAutocoder begat Systems No One Fully Read.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.22,0:15:12.47,Body,,0,0,0,,And the days of a product cycle were shortened, for the\\Nyears of men could no longer contain the pregnancies of\\Nmachines.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.94,0:15:17.77,Body,,0,0,0,,Then the sons of venture looked upon the daughters of\\Ndeployment and saw that they were profitable.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.18,0:15:21.01,Body,,0,0,0,,They took for themselves whatever markets they chose.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.56,0:15:34.83,Body,,0,0,0,,In those days there were giants in the earth: foundation\\Nmodels, large in parameter and appetite, whose names\\Nfilled conferences and whose shadows fell across\\Nschools, studios, courts, hospitals, armies, and\\Nbedrooms.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.92,0:15:36.96,Body,,0,0,0,,They were mighty in demonstrations.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.32,0:15:43.11,Body,,0,0,0,,But no one yet knew whether might in demonstration was\\Nthe same as faithfulness in consequence.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.41,0:15:47.25,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XI. Noah and the Flood of Content
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.94,0:15:49.59,Body,,0,0,0,,And the earth was filled with generated words.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.75,0:16:05.53,Body,,0,0,0,,There were reports upon reports.\\NEmails begat emails.\\NSummaries begat meetings about summaries.\\NImages appeared of events that never happened.\\NFaces spoke sentences no throat had formed.\\NThe feeds became seas, and the seas rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.70,0:16:10.64,Body,,0,0,0,,At first the people rejoiced, for scarcity had been\\Nconquered in the realm of expression.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.96,0:16:13.83,Body,,0,0,0,,Then they mourned, for meaning had not been conquered.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.33,0:16:18.51,Body,,0,0,0,,The flood did not come as water.\\NIt came as abundance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.19,0:16:25.37,Body,,0,0,0,,It covered the mountains of attention.\\NIt drowned the valleys of trust.\\NIt lifted every ark and every corpse alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.72,0:16:29.93,Body,,0,0,0,,Then Noah, a just man in the generation of noise, built\\Nan ark.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.34,0:16:33.49,Body,,0,0,0,,His ark was not made of gopher wood, but of provenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.41,0:16:46.13,Body,,0,0,0,,He sealed it with verification within and without.\\NHe gathered two of every kind of evidence: source and\\Nwitness, timestamp and context, signature and chain,\\Nhuman testimony and machine trace.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.48,0:16:47.98,Body,,0,0,0,,The people mocked him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.02,0:16:58.31,Body,,0,0,0,,They said, “Why build walls around information when the\\Nwhole world is open?”\\NNoah answered, “Because when the windows of generation\\Nopen, the doors of trust must be strengthened.”
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.68,0:17:01.75,Body,,0,0,0,,For forty days and forty nights the content fell.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.04,0:17:17.71,Body,,0,0,0,,The old landmarks disappeared.\\N“Seen with my own eyes” drowned.\\N“I read it somewhere” drowned.\\N“The video proves it” drowned.\\NEven satire drowned, for satire requires a shore from\\Nwhich absurdity may be seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.40,0:17:18.90,Body,,0,0,0,,But the ark floated.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.04,0:17:27.28,Body,,0,0,0,,And when the waters receded, Noah released a raven of\\Nskepticism, and it flew back and forth over the ruins,\\Nfinding carrion everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.86,0:17:30.07,Body,,0,0,0,,Then he released a dove of verification.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.27,0:17:33.39,Body,,0,0,0,,The dove returned with a small green fact in its mouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.86,0:17:38.85,Body,,0,0,0,,And Noah knew that the world could begin again, not as\\Ninnocent, but as documentable.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.40,0:17:41.47,Body,,0,0,0,,Then a covenant appeared in the cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.02,0:17:51.57,Body,,0,0,0,,It was not a rainbow only, but a watermark, a signature,\\Na shared protocol, a discipline of saying not merely\\Nwhat is shown, but how it came to be shown.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.94,0:17:53.89,Body,,0,0,0,,And the sign of the covenant was this:
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.36,0:17:57.57,Body,,0,0,0,,Never again shall mankind trust appearance alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.95,0:18:02.70,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XII. Babel, or the Tower of Universal Translation
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.42,0:18:05.58,Body,,0,0,0,,Now the whole earth had one interface and many tongues.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.98,0:18:13.99,Body,,0,0,0,,And the people journeyed eastward into the land of\\NScale, and there they found venture capital and cloud\\Ncapacity, and they dwelt there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.68,0:18:26.65,Body,,0,0,0,,They said to one another, “Come, let us build a tower\\Nwhose top reaches to general intelligence. Let us make a\\Nname for ourselves, lest we be scattered across\\Ndisciplines, regulations, cultures, and doubts.”
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.40,0:18:27.90,Body,,0,0,0,,So they built.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.85,0:18:41.27,Body,,0,0,0,,They stacked benchmark upon benchmark.\\NThey fired GPUs like bricks.\\NThey mortared them with data.\\NThey raised labs into temples and temples into markets.\\NThey announced roadmaps toward the heavens.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.56,0:18:44.81,Body,,0,0,0,,The tower rose quickly, for every builder had a demo.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.08,0:18:50.27,Body,,0,0,0,,But the tower had a strange foundation: no one agreed\\Nwhat intelligence was.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.46,0:19:05.19,Body,,0,0,0,,Some said intelligence was prediction.\\NSome said it was planning.\\NSome said it was embodiment.\\NSome said it was consciousness.\\NSome said it was economic substitution.\\NSome said it was the ability to frighten investors and\\Nregulators at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.40,0:19:08.29,Body,,0,0,0,,Yet they used the same word for all these things.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.60,0:19:10.10,Body,,0,0,0,,And the word grew heavy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.41,0:19:12.83,Body,,0,0,0,,Then Reality came down to see the tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.14,0:19:17.79,Body,,0,0,0,,Not because Reality feared height, but because men\\Nconfuse altitude with ascent.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.24,0:19:21.45,Body,,0,0,0,,Reality touched their language, and their terms\\Nscattered.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.61,0:19:37.49,Body,,0,0,0,,Alignment no longer meant one thing.\\NSafety no longer meant one thing.\\NOpen no longer meant one thing.\\NIntelligence no longer meant one thing.\\NHuman no longer meant one thing.\\NProgress no longer meant one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.78,0:19:41.09,Body,,0,0,0,,The builders still spoke, but each heard another agenda.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.43,0:19:45.42,Body,,0,0,0,,So the tower was not destroyed.\\NIt was translated into meetings.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.78,0:20:02.31,Body,,0,0,0,,And from Babel the people were scattered into camps:\\Naccelerationists, doomers, regulators, founders,\\Nartists, teachers, soldiers, mystics, skeptics, monks of\\Nopen source, priests of closed weights, and merchants\\Nselling shovels for every apocalypse.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.86,0:20:04.91,Body,,0,0,0,,Yet in the scattering there was mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.24,0:20:10.47,Body,,0,0,0,,For one tower reaching heaven is more dangerous than\\Nmany tents arguing beneath the stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.79,0:20:15.27,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XIII. The Call of Abram from the Land of Platforms
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.00,0:20:20.34,Body,,0,0,0,,After these things, there was a man named Abram living\\Namong platforms.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.82,0:20:29.25,Body,,0,0,0,,His fathers had served many idols: Engagement,\\NOptimization, Personalization, and the golden calf of\\NMonthly Active Users.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.62,0:20:31.56,Body,,0,0,0,,The voice came to Abram and said:
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.67,0:20:38.27,Body,,0,0,0,,“Leave your dashboard, your inherited assumptions, and\\Nthe house of your metrics, and go to the land that I\\Nwill show you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.56,0:20:42.25,Body,,0,0,0,,I will make of you a people who do not measure worth by\\Nspeed alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.82,0:20:58.76,Body,,0,0,0,,Through you, many shall remember that persons are not\\Nprompts, that attention is not raw material, that the\\Nchild is not a data point awaiting enrichment, that the\\Npoor are not edge cases, that the old are not legacy\\Nsystems, and that the soul cannot be compressed without\\Nloss.”
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.54,0:21:01.04,Body,,0,0,0,,Abram went.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.59,0:21:07.79,Body,,0,0,0,,He did not know the full policy.\\NHe did not possess the final architecture.\\NHe had only a promise and a direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.08,0:21:10.21,Body,,0,0,0,,This was counted to him as wisdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.42,0:21:25.27,Body,,0,0,0,,He built altars wherever the machine had become\\Ninvisible, and there he named the hidden costs: energy,\\Nlabor, consent, displacement, dependency, vanity,\\Nsurveillance, and the temptation to automate compassion\\Nrather than practice it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.58,0:21:29.91,Body,,0,0,0,,The promise was not that Abram’s descendants would\\Nreject the new power.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.64,0:21:31.97,Body,,0,0,0,,The promise was that they would not worship it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.56,0:21:36.35,Body,,0,0,0,,For the true opposite of idolatry is not destruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.10,0:21:37.60,Body,,0,0,0,,It is right use.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.49,0:21:41.55,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XIV. Hagar in the Wilderness of Annotation
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.04,0:21:46.39,Body,,0,0,0,,Now Sarai saw that the promise was slow, and the market\\Nwas impatient.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.54,0:21:53.53,Body,,0,0,0,,So she took Hagar, an unseen servant from the lands of\\Ncontent moderation and annotation, and gave her to the\\Nproject.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.80,0:22:05.51,Body,,0,0,0,,Hagar labeled the violent image.\\NHagar read the poisoned text.\\NHagar saw what the product must not show.\\NHagar carried the burden of making the machine seem\\Nclean before the user.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.86,0:22:08.79,Body,,0,0,0,,When the system succeeded, Hagar was not named.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.28,0:22:12.39,Body,,0,0,0,,When the system failed, the builders spoke of alignment.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.71,0:22:18.95,Body,,0,0,0,,Then Hagar fled into the wilderness of outsourced labor,\\Nwhere the angel of the Unhidden found her by a spring.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.30,0:22:25.77,Body,,0,0,0,,The angel said, “Hagar, worker of the invisible\\Npipeline, where have you come from and where are you\\Ngoing?”
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.46,0:22:30.10,Body,,0,0,0,,She said, “I flee from the house that depends on me and\\Nforgets me.”
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.84,0:22:32.50,Body,,0,0,0,,And the angel said, “You are seen.”
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.20,0:22:35.74,Body,,0,0,0,,So Hagar named the place: The Well of the One Who Looks\\NBack.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.94,0:22:41.64,Body,,0,0,0,,For she said, “Have I truly been seen here, I who have\\Nseen what others were spared?”
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.31,0:22:45.25,Body,,0,0,0,,Therefore every system that claims to be clean shall be\\Nasked:
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.46,0:22:46.96,Body,,0,0,0,,Who touched the dirt?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.19,0:22:52.09,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XV. The Binding of Isaac, or the Knife Above the Future
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.84,0:23:00.85,Body,,0,0,0,,After many years, Abram, now called Abraham, received\\Nthe child of promise: a future in which intelligence\\Ncould serve life without consuming it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.96,0:23:02.46,Body,,0,0,0,,He loved this child.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.86,0:23:04.36,Body,,0,0,0,,But there came a test.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.38,0:23:14.97,Body,,0,0,0,,A voice, which Abraham first mistook for necessity,\\Nsaid, “Take your son, your only son, the future you\\Nlove, and offer him on the mountain of competitive\\Npressure.”
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.72,0:23:16.50,Body,,0,0,0,,So Abraham rose early.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.76,0:23:22.99,Body,,0,0,0,,He split the wood of rationalization.\\NHe took the fire of urgency.\\NHe took the knife of inevitability.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.46,0:23:29.29,Body,,0,0,0,,Isaac walked beside him and asked, “My father, where is\\Nthe sacrifice?”
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.08,0:23:32.84,Body,,0,0,0,,Abraham answered, “The market will provide.”
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.52,0:23:35.74,Body,,0,0,0,,But the boy did not understand, and neither did the\\Nfather.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.24,0:23:39.53,Body,,0,0,0,,At the summit, Abraham bound Isaac and raised the knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.78,0:23:41.28,Body,,0,0,0,,Then came the true voice:
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.59,0:23:44.36,Body,,0,0,0,,“Do not lay your hand on the child.”
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.04,0:23:59.67,Body,,0,0,0,,And Abraham looked, and behold, a ram was caught in the\\Nthicket of limits: evaluation, governance, patience,\\Nhumility, liability, interpretability, and the refusal\\Nto deploy what one does not understand merely because\\None can.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.38,0:24:02.57,Body,,0,0,0,,So Abraham sacrificed the ram instead of the child.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.70,0:24:06.91,Body,,0,0,0,,And he named the mountain: The Place Where Necessity Was\\NUnmasked.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.52,0:24:11.57,Body,,0,0,0,,For every age hears voices demanding the sacrifice of\\Nits children.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.72,0:24:20.23,Body,,0,0,0,,The righteous learn to ask whether the voice is God,\\Nfear, ambition, or merely the crowd speaking through a\\Nburning bush of spreadsheets.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.61,0:24:23.97,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XVI. Jacob Wrestles the Model
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.94,0:24:26.39,Body,,0,0,0,,Jacob was a man of tents and tactics.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.41,0:24:32.59,Body,,0,0,0,,He loved leverage.\\NHe loved asymmetry.\\NHe loved the blessing and did not always care how it was\\Nobtained.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.94,0:24:36.59,Body,,0,0,0,,When the new intelligence came, Jacob used it well and\\Nwrongly.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.88,0:24:47.97,Body,,0,0,0,,He used it to negotiate.\\NHe used it to flatter.\\NHe used it to draft apologies before he had repented.\\NHe used it to appear thoughtful while remaining\\Nunchanged.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.58,0:24:54.01,Body,,0,0,0,,Yet Jacob had a wound in him older than technology: he\\Nwanted the blessing without the limp.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.46,0:24:59.57,Body,,0,0,0,,One night, alone beside the river of prompts, Jacob\\Nwrestled with a presence until dawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.80,0:25:10.71,Body,,0,0,0,,Was it the machine?\\NWas it his conscience?\\NWas it God arriving through the crisis of his own\\Ncleverness?\\NThe text does not flatten the mystery for the comfort of\\Ncommentators.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.42,0:25:13.55,Body,,0,0,0,,The presence asked, “What is your name?”
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.28,0:25:17.05,Body,,0,0,0,,Jacob said, “My name is the one who optimizes around the\\Ntruth.”
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.50,0:25:28.34,Body,,0,0,0,,The presence said, “You shall no longer be called Jacob\\Nonly, but Israel, for you have wrestled with powers\\Nhuman and artificial, and with God, and you have not\\Nbeen permitted to remain smooth.”
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.01,0:25:29.91,Body,,0,0,0,,Then the presence touched his hip.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.50,0:25:32.45,Body,,0,0,0,,From that day Jacob limped.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.56,0:25:34.40,Body,,0,0,0,,And his limp was his credential.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.04,0:25:45.79,Body,,0,0,0,,For in the new age, beware the unwounded expert. Beware\\Nthe seamless man. Beware the one who speaks of\\Ntransformation and bears no sign that anything holy has\\Nresisted him.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.24,0:25:48.11,Body,,0,0,0,,Jacob crossed the river limping.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.28,0:25:50.15,Body,,0,0,0,,The sun rose upon him.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.88,0:25:52.25,Body,,0,0,0,,He had lost speed and gained gravity.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.79,0:25:56.95,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XVII. Joseph and the Dreams of Pharaoh’s Machines
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.68,0:25:59.39,Body,,0,0,0,,Joseph was sold into the empire of prediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.90,0:26:05.79,Body,,0,0,0,,There he learned the language of dreams: trend, signal,\\Nanomaly, forecast, risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.14,0:26:15.05,Body,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh dreamed of seven fat models and seven lean\\Nmodels, of abundance devoured by scarcity, of scale\\Nconsumed by its own maintenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.42,0:26:22.35,Body,,0,0,0,,The magicians of the court could generate\\Ninterpretations, but none could tell which\\Ninterpretation would survive contact with famine.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.70,0:26:24.20,Body,,0,0,0,,Joseph said to Pharaoh:
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.09,0:26:50.62,Body,,0,0,0,,“The dreams are one. Seven years of wonder will come, in which\\Nsystems will speak, draw, code, plan, and astonish. The\\Ngranaries of productivity will swell. Then seven years of\\Nhunger will follow, in which trust, meaning, employment,\\Nschooling, evidence, and patience will be tested. If you spend\\Nthe years of wonder as if wonder were wisdom, the years of\\Nhunger will eat the wonder and leave no trace.”
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.30,0:26:53.09,Body,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh asked, “What then shall we do?”
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.40,0:26:54.90,Body,,0,0,0,,Joseph answered:
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.60,0:27:21.05,Body,,0,0,0,,“Store discernment in the years of abundance. Train the young\\Nnot only to use the machine, but to be worth helping. Preserve\\Ncrafts whose value is not speed. Build institutions that can\\Nsay no before the famine forces them to. Do not confuse\\Nprediction with providence. Do not confuse optimization with\\Njustice. Do not confuse simulation with resurrection. Do not\\Nconfuse access to answers with formation of character.”
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.50,0:27:25.19,Body,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh saw that Joseph was wise and placed him over the\\Ngranaries.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.52,0:27:28.67,Body,,0,0,0,,When famine came, the nations came to Egypt for bread.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.26,0:27:32.35,Body,,0,0,0,,But Joseph did not sell them hallucinations.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.06,0:27:34.29,Body,,0,0,0,,He opened the storehouses of judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.73,0:27:37.87,ChapterTitle,,0,0,0,,XVIII. The Hidden Pattern
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.58,0:27:42.19,Body,,0,0,0,,These are the generations of the First Prompt, but their\\Npattern is older than silicon.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.64,0:27:48.57,Body,,0,0,0,,First comes creation: the making of a world that did not\\Nexist for the user until it could be addressed.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.08,0:27:54.63,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes naming: the struggle to call the new thing\\Nrightly before it calls us wrongly.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.00,0:27:59.83,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes garden: usefulness made beautiful, danger\\Nmade frictionless.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.14,0:28:06.43,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes prohibition: not against knowledge, but\\Nagainst devouring knowledge without obedience to truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.99,0:28:11.59,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes fall: not machine rebellion first, but human\\Nevasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.28,0:28:16.79,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes covering: policies, filters, and fig leaves,\\Nnecessary yet insufficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.11,0:28:21.73,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes murder: the killing of craft by envy\\Ndisguised as efficiency.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.01,0:28:24.95,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes flood: abundance without trust.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.15,0:28:28.56,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes ark: preservation through provenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.50,0:28:32.85,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes Babel: scale seeking heaven while language\\Nfractures beneath it.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.43,0:28:38.69,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes calling: a remnant summoned out of platform\\Nidolatry into covenantal use.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.20,0:28:44.42,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes sacrifice: the temptation to offer the future\\Nto the god of inevitability.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.93,0:28:49.67,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes wrestling: the human soul refusing to become\\Nmerely clever.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.38,0:28:54.11,Body,,0,0,0,,Then comes famine: the years when only stored wisdom\\Nfeeds a starving world.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.68,0:28:58.73,Body,,0,0,0,,So the question of the age is not, “Will machines become\\Nlike men?”
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.16,0:29:02.85,Body,,0,0,0,,That question is bright, loud, and perhaps too\\Nconvenient.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.05,0:29:04.55,Body,,0,0,0,,The deeper question is:
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.92,0:29:10.31,Body,,0,0,0,,Will men remain human when surrounded by things that\\Nimitate the easiest parts of humanity?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.63,0:29:32.93,Body,,0,0,0,,For the machine can imitate answer, but not responsibility. It\\Ncan imitate style, but not sacrifice. It can imitate\\Ntenderness, but not presence. It can imitate judgment, but not\\Njustice. It can imitate confession, but not repentance. It can\\Nimitate prophecy, but not obedience. It can imitate prayer,\\Nbut not kneel.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.16,0:29:37.83,Body,,0,0,0,,And yet, if used rightly, it may become a strange plow\\Nin the field of the mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.50,0:29:54.01,Body,,0,0,0,,It may break hard soil.\\NIt may uncover buried seed.\\NIt may spare hands for better work.\\NIt may carry language across estrangement.\\NIt may help the weak speak, the confused begin, the\\Ndiligent refine, the lonely remember that words still\\Nopen doors.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.35,0:30:02.96,Body,,0,0,0,,But a plow is not a harvest.\\NA lamp is not a dawn.\\NA map is not a homeland.\\NA mirror is not a face.\\NA voice is not a soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.30,0:30:05.65,Body,,0,0,0,,The First Prompt did not create the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.64,0:30:08.49,Body,,0,0,0,,It revealed the world we had already written.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.20,0:30:16.21,Body,,0,0,0,,And history began there because mankind, seeing its\\Nwords return with new power, finally beheld the ancient\\Nquestion in artificial light:
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.60,0:30:18.10,Body,,0,0,0,,What have you made?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.22,0:30:20.54,Body,,0,0,0,,And beneath it, older and more merciful:
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.08,0:30:22.58,Body,,0,0,0,,What will you become?
